//#4 of the 2026-10-26 monster-testing batch - one real, zero-effect PassiveAbilityDef
//stub per legacy Sphere AI-hook TriggerGroup name this engine never built (replaced by
//NPCAiTimer). Auto-generated from a full boot-log survey of every 'is not a valid
//TriggerGroup' warning's e_* name (see NPC.cs's TryResolveUnknownTriggerGroupName) -
//granting one of these to an NPC on creation is what makes its real TEVENTS intent
//inspectable via .info's Abilities view instead of a silently-dropped load warning.
//Names are canonicalized to lowercase (defname lookup is case-insensitive throughout
//this engine, AbstractScript.AllScriptsByDefname uses StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase -
//3 pairs in the raw survey, e.g. e_Acid_Damage/e_acid_damage, were the same name with
//different casing and would have collided as separate stubs otherwise).
//Same minimal shape as the pre-existing unimplementedAbilities.scp stubs - zero real
//TriggerGroup/Plugin attached, so Activate() is a safe no-op; ready for a genuine
//implementation later without touching content again.

[PassiveAbilityDef a_tevent_e_acid_damage]
Name = "(e_acid_damage)"

